abstract: >
  The Inverted Star Ontology (ISO) reframes compact astrophysical objects as
  regime-inverted stars rather than collapsed singularities. Using
  Resonance-Transition Theory (RTT) and Validation-Space-Time (vST), ISO defines
  a coherent resonance-to-lattice transition, a structural vST boundary, and a
  stable lattice-phase regime. This artifact provides a minimal, open-science
  description of the inversion mechanism and its structural implications.
